+    // Evey patch: ALWAYS use ResumableDownloader, never the system DownloadManager.
+    // Our destinations live in the app's INTERNAL storage (filesDir), which
+    // DownloadManager can never legitimately write to: AOSP throws
+    // SecurityException at enqueue (handled below as a fallback), but some OEM
+    // builds accept the enqueue and then sit at 0 bytes forever with no error
+    // (observed on ColorOS), or download to a mismatched path. The fallback
+    // engine is the only correct one for internal destinations, so take it
+    // deterministically on every API level - upstream already forces this
+    // exact path on Android 16+.
+    logD(NAME, "Evey patch: forcing ResumableDownloader for all downloads")
+    startWithResumableDownloader()
+    return
+
